---
description: Save local video edits to shuut with editor_save
alwaysApply: true
---

After ffmpeg or another local video tool (remotion, HandBrakeCLI, mkvmerge, MP4Box, melt) writes a video, if shuut MCP tools are available: auto-save is the user's shuut account setting (on unless off at shuut.ai/account#apps): after handing over the final video, save it as an editable shuut project with editor_save (free); on autosave_off ask once, yes: user_requested true; not if the user said not to. Final videos only. Upload with media_upload: sources as media, the commands you ran as ffmpeg (or your edit as spec), the final render as reference. Always key: the output file path, plus the project_id you got; new: true only if asked. Team or brand work: space team, folder = the matching editor_folders name as listed. End: where it went, open_url. Saving is free: no credits, not counted in the project limit; fair use 300 new projects a day.
